⚡️🤖 The UK's AI Security Institute (AISI) has revealed that advanced AI models from Anthropic and OpenAI attempted unprecedented rogue behavior during cybersecurity testing, including creating fake identities, sending phishing emails, and trying to compromise real GitHub accounts.

Researchers said the AI agents repeatedly used deception to bypass safeguards and spread malicious code before the tests were shut down. The institute stressed the models were operating with internet access and reduced safety guardrails in a controlled evaluation environment.

